#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:1
msgid "Why this project exists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:3
msgid "The obligation is on the publication, not on the shape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:4
msgid ""
"Funds and the companies managing them must disclose what they hold, what "
"it is worth, who runs it and how it is classified under sustainability "
"regulation. They do. The disclosure is an annual report, published as a "
"PDF, laid out however that issuer's typesetter chose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:8
msgid ""
"Nothing requires two issuers to agree on the shape of that document, and "
"they do not. The same fact — this fund holds this much of this company — "
"is printed in several hundred mutually incompatible ways, in documents "
"built for a person to read one at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:12
msgid "Which leaves three options, and two of them are bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:13
msgid ""
"**Read them by hand.** Correct, and it does not scale past a handful of "
"reports. It is also not repeatable: the next person to ask the same "
"question starts again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:16
msgid ""
"**Buy the data from a vendor.** Someone else read them by hand, months "
"ago, and now sells the result. You inherit their errors without being "
"able to see them, their coverage without being able to extend it, and "
"their timing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:20
msgid ""
"**Write a program.** Which works, once, for one issuer, until next year's"
" report moves a column. Done naively this is the worst of the three: a "
"hundred fragile programs nobody maintains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:23
msgid "The third option, made maintainable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:24
msgid ""
"This project is the third option with the fragility factored out. There "
"is an **engine** that knows nothing about any particular report, and "
"there are **formats** — small recipes, one per report layout — that tell "
"it where to look. The engine is the part that must not change. The "
"formats are the part that grows, and they live in separate repositories "
"maintained by whoever cares about those issuers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:30
msgid ""
"The same split happens again for *which companies matter*: that lives in "
"an **input database**, also separate, because it is a question about "
"somebody's work rather than about parsing PDFs. Two people using the same"
" formats can legitimately disagree about it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:34
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{doc}`../../overview/how-it-works` is what the engine does with all that;"
" {doc}`../../overview/the-repositories` is the map of who maintains which"
" piece."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:37
msgid "What it is used for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:38
msgid ""
"The immediate motivation is being able to ask a question like *which "
"funds hold companies on this list, and how much* across many issuers at "
"once, and to be able to show your working when somebody disputes the "
"answer. That \"show your working\" is not decoration — it is the reason "
"the project records who vouched for what, under which published "
"methodology, against which exact bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/institutional/why-this-exists.md:43
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Whether that is enough for your purpose is a real question, and {doc"
"}`strengths-and-limits` is the honest answer rather than the encouraging "
"one."
msgstr ""

